WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
A summer evening in the Lake District.

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.760
A boy unties a boat that isn't his.

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.050
He pushes off, and rows
out across the still lake,

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.350
proud of every stroke.

5
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.010
Then, from behind the ridge,
a huge black peak looms up.

6
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.170
He turns back, fast.

7
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.010
For days, huge shapes fill
his thoughts and dreams.

8
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.620
Why would a mountain haunt a boy?

9
00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll feel how
the theft starts as a thrill,

10
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.320
with guilt underneath.

11
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.100
You'll find the turning point,
where confidence becomes fear.

12
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.580
And you'll see why this memory,
from Book I of The Prelude,

13
00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.320
stayed with Wordsworth all his life.

14
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.880
Your mission: work out why
the mountain haunts him.
